<h2 class="g-h2" id="usage">Usage</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>Put the list in a <code>&lt;dd data-cite-cell&gt;</code>. <code>cite_fit.js</code> measures that cell and hides, from the end, every entry that would overflow it or wrap; the button then says how many are hidden. Narrow the window and the count changes. In an inline cell (no <code>data-cite-cell</code>, as in a tab row's detail line) the first <code>limit</code> entries show and nothing is measured.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="parameters">Parameters</h2>
{{ params([
  ["items", "string[]", "", "The entries, in order."],
  ["limit", "number", "3", "How many are candidates to show before the button."],
  ["dot", "boolean", "false", "Separate entries with a middle dot instead of a comma."],
  ["noun", "string", "\"citation\"", "Names the entries in the button's label: \"Show 2 more case numbers\"."]
]) }}

<h2 class="g-h2" id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>The button is an Alpine <code>listToggle</code> (<code>composables/list_toggle.js</code>). Expanding adds <code>is-expanded</code> to the cell, which shows every entry; collapsing dispatches <code>cite-list:collapse</code> so <code>cite_fit.js</code> fits the line again. The list keeps no state of its own. Without script the first <code>limit</code> entries show.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The button is a native <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> with <code>aria-expanded</code> and a label that counts what it reveals. Test it with text zoom: fitting re-runs whenever the cell changes size.</p></div>

